IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Singapore Broadcasting Authority (TVRO System) (Amendment) Regulations 2001 (S 354/2001), made under s 79 of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297), the Broadcasting Act's former name.
-- Deposit: ../../../singapore-broadcasting-authority-tvro-system-amendment-regulations-2001/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S354-2001.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited).
-- First published 23 July 2001 at 5:00 pm; made 17 July 2001; "shall come into operation on 1st August 2001". It amends the TVRO System Regulations (Rg 3), encoded in the Revised Edition 2004 in `sgba-i-tvro-regs.l4`.
-- The new regulations 3 to 5, 8 and 9 are printed whole; each is identical in substance to the text the Revised Edition 2004 prints (same words as `sgba-i-tvro-regs.l4`), which is why the Revised Edition's text is the text from 1 August 2001 if nothing amended it between (its amendment note lists S 354/2001 as the last).

§ `Paragraph 3: regulations 3, 4 and 5 substituted`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 23rd July 2001 at 5:00 pm.
-- src:21 | Citation and commencement
-- src:22 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Singapore Broadcasting
-- src:23 | Authority (TVRO System) (Amendment) Regulations 2001 and
-- src:24 | shall come into operation on 1st August 2001.
@ref S 354/2001 publication line and para 1 (commencement) (src:3-24)
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 the substituted regulations are in operation on` MEANS
    `the day of the conduct` AT LEAST (Date 1 8 2001)

-- src:43 | Deletion and substitution of regulations 3, 4 and 5
-- src:44 | 3. Regulations 3, 4 and 5 of the principal Regulations are deleted
-- src:45 | and the following regulations substituted therefor:
-- src:46 | ‘‘Application and qualifications
-- src:47 | 3.—(1) An application for a licence —
-- src:48 | (a) shall be made in such form and manner as the Authority
-- src:49 | may determine; and
-- src:50 | (b) shall contain a full and true account of such particulars
-- src:51 | as the Authority may require.
-- src:52 | (2) No person other than an institution may be granted with
-- src:53 | a licence.
@ref S 354/2001 para 3: new reg 3(1) and (2) (application and qualifications) (src:43-53)
GIVEN `the application is made in the form and manner the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a full and true account of the particulars the Authority required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 reg 3(1) the application for a licence is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the application is made in the form and manner the Authority determined` AND `the application contains a full and true account of the particulars the Authority required`

GIVEN `it is a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 reg 3(2) the person may be granted a licence` MEANS
    `it is a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` OR `it is an undertaking`

-- src:55 | Licence fee
-- src:56 | 4.—(1) The Authority may refuse to grant or renew any
-- src:57 | licence unless such fee as the Authority may determine to be
-- src:58 | levied in respect of the licence is paid.
-- src:59 | (2) No fee or part thereof paid in respect of any licence
-- src:60 | granted by the Authority shall be refunded in respect of the
-- src:61 | unexpired period of any licence which has been cancelled or
-- src:62 | suspended in accordance with section 33, read with section 24,
-- src:63 | of the Act.
@ref S 354/2001 para 3: new reg 4 (licence fee) (src:55-63)
GIVEN `the fee the Authority determined to be levied in respect of the licence has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 reg 4(1) the Authority may refuse to grant or renew the licence` MEANS
    NOT `the fee the Authority determined to be levied in respect of the licence has been paid`

GIVEN `the licence has been cancelled or suspended in accordance with section 33, read with section 24, of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 reg 4(2) no fee or part of it is refunded for the unexpired period` MEANS
    `the licence has been cancelled or suspended in accordance with section 33, read with section 24, of the Act`

-- src:65 | Period of licence
-- src:66 | 5. A licence shall be valid for such period as the Authority
-- src:67 | may determine unless it is sooner cancelled or suspended.’’.
@ref S 354/2001 para 3: new reg 5 (period of licence) (src:65-67)
GIVEN `the Authority determined a period for the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence has been sooner cancelled or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 reg 5 the licence is valid` MEANS
    `the Authority determined a period for the licence` AND (NOT `the licence has been sooner cancelled or suspended`)

-- src:72 | ‘‘Changes to or inaccuracy in particulars
-- src:73 | 8. A licensee shall inform the Authority in writing of any
-- src:74 | change to or inaccuracy in any of its particulars furnished to
-- src:75 | the Authority under regulation 3 (1) (b).
@ref S 354/2001 para 4: new reg 8 (changes to or inaccuracy in particulars) (src:72-75)
GIVEN `there is a change to or inaccuracy in a particular the licensee furnished under regulation 3(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee informed the Authority in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 reg 8 the licensee has complied` MEANS
    (NOT `there is a change to or inaccuracy in a particular the licensee furnished under regulation 3(1)(b)`) OR `the licensee informed the Authority in writing`

-- src:78 | Surrender of licence
-- src:79 | 9. A person whose licence is cancelled or suspended under
-- src:80 | section 33, read with section 24, of the Act shall, if required by
-- src:81 | the Authority, surrender the licence to the Authority within
-- src:82 | such time as the Authority may specify.’’.
@ref S 354/2001 para 4: new reg 9 (surrender of licence) (src:78-82)
GIVEN `the licence is cancelled or suspended under section 33, read with section 24, of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority requires the licence to be surrendered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 reg 9 the person must surrender the licence within the time the Authority specifies` MEANS
    `the licence is cancelled or suspended under section 33, read with section 24, of the Act` AND `the Authority requires the licence to be surrendered`

-- src:27 | 2. Regulation 2 of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority (TVRO
-- src:28 | System) Regulations (Rg 3) (referred to in these Regulations as the
-- src:29 | principal Regulations) is amended —
-- src:30 | (a) by deleting the definition of ‘‘broadcast television receiver’’
-- src:31 | and substituting the following definition:
-- src:32 | ‘‘ ‘‘broadcast television receiver’’ means any apparatus
-- src:33 | used for the visual and aural reception of any
-- src:34 | broadcasting service;’’; and
-- src:35 | (b) by deleting the definitions of ‘‘licence’’ and ‘‘licensee’’ and
-- src:36 | substituting the following definitions:
-- src:37 | ‘‘ ‘‘licence’’ means a licence to install or operate one
-- src:38 | or more TVRO systems;
-- src:39 | ‘‘licensee’’ means a person to whom a licence is
-- src:40 | granted;’’.
@ref S 354/2001 para 2: reg 2 amended ("broadcast television receiver", "licence", "licensee") (src:27-40)
GIVEN `it is an apparatus used for the visual and aural reception of any broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 reg 2 the apparatus is a broadcast television receiver` MEANS
    `it is an apparatus used for the visual and aural reception of any broadcasting service`

GIVEN `it is a licence to install or operate one or more TVRO systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 reg 2 the licence is a licence within the Regulations` MEANS
    `it is a licence to install or operate one or more TVRO systems`

GIVEN `a licence has been granted to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 354/2001 reg 2 the person is a licensee` MEANS
    `a licence has been granted to the person`

-- S 354/2001 para 5 (deposit lines 85-95) replaces "issued" with "granted", "worked" and "work" with "operated" and "operate", and "working" with "operation" in regulations 6(1), 10, 11, 12 and 14: wording changes; no rule is stated here.
